<title>SWEDEN: Ex-Astra employee calls sex case a set-up.</title>
<headline>Ex-Astra employee calls sex case a set-up.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lars Bildman, the former Astra managing director who was fired after allegations of sexual harassment, on Tuesday accused Astra's managing director Hakan Mogren of plotting a conspiracy against him.</p>
<p>&quot;I am quite sure about that,&quot; Bildman, former president of Astra's U.S. division, told a Swedish television interview.</p>
<p>Astra rejected the accusations.</p>
<p>&quot;This is a completely preposterous accusation,&quot; Astra spokesman Staffan Ternby told the channel TV4.</p>
<p>Astra in April announced the suspension of Bildman pending an internal investigation into sexual harassment and financial improprieties.</p>
<p>He was sacked in June.</p>
<p>Bildman has denied allegations in a lawsuit from a former sales trainee with Astra USA that he made unwanted sexual advances towards her during her time with the firm.</p>
<p>-- Erik Aronsson, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1010</p>
